{"id":"8c378d927a6403cc","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-thm-baire-category-theory.md","title":"Baire Category Theory","display":"thm-baire-category-theory — Baire Category Theory","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-baire-category-theory","aliases":["58-thm-baire-category-theory","Baire Category Theorem General","Baire Space Theory"],"display":"thm-baire-category-theory — Baire Category Theory","depends_on":["[[58-df-complete-metric]]","[[58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space]]","[[58-thm-baire-category]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-baire-category-theory"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-baire-category-theory</span><span>Baire Category Theorem General</span><span>Baire Space Theory</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-baire-category-theory — Baire Category Theory"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"05d80cd20b53d8a2\" href=\"?note=05d80cd20b53d8a2\" title=\"58-df-complete-metric\">58-df-complete-metric</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7ba0d54b1c8a5fbf\" href=\"?note=7ba0d54b1c8a5fbf\" title=\"58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space\">58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"92a68d008dd67859\" href=\"?note=92a68d008dd67859\" title=\"58-thm-baire-category\">58-thm-baire-category</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,d,\\tau_d\\in V\">\\(X,d,\\tau_d\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"05d80cd20b53d8a2\" href=\"?note=05d80cd20b53d8a2\" title=\"58-df-complete-metric\">58-df-complete-metric</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTopo8BaireCategorySpace}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTopo8BaireCategorySpace}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"7ba0d54b1c8a5fbf\" href=\"?note=7ba0d54b1c8a5fbf\" title=\"58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space\">58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}baire\\text{-}category\\text{-}theory} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\n\\land \\tau_d=\n\\left\\{O\\subseteq X:\n\\forall x\\in O\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(\\langle x,y\\rangle)&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in O)\n\\right\\}\n\\to \\mathrm{ZfcTopo8BaireCategorySpace}_S(X,\\tau_d)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}baire\\text{-}category\\text{-}theory} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\n\\land \\tau_d=\n\\left\\{O\\subseteq X:\n\\forall x\\in O\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(\\langle x,y\\rangle)&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in O)\n\\right\\}\n\\to \\mathrm{ZfcTopo8BaireCategorySpace}_S(X,\\tau_d)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The premise explicitly identifies <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_d\">\\(\\tau_d\\)</span> with the topology induced by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span>; completeness alone cannot imply the conclusion for an arbitrary unrelated topology.  The metric graph is applied to ordered pairs, matching its registered set-function domain <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\times X\">\\(X\\times X\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Meager subsets of a Baire space have empty interior.</li>\n<li>The Banach-Mazur game gives a game-theoretic characterization of non-meagerness.</li>\n<li>Meagerness and measure zero are distinct notions of smallness.</li>\n<li>Applications: functional analysis, topology.</li>\n<li>Baire property: sets approximable by open (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"b5b9f71b20826f2d\" href=\"?note=b5b9f71b20826f2d\" title=\"58-df-baire-property\">58-df-baire-property</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-complete-metric","status":"resolved","id":"05d80cd20b53d8a2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-complete-metric]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space","status":"resolved","id":"7ba0d54b1c8a5fbf","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-thm-baire-category","status":"resolved","id":"92a68d008dd67859","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-thm-baire-category]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-complete-metric","status":"resolved","id":"05d80cd20b53d8a2","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[58-df-complete-metric]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space","status":"resolved","id":"7ba0d54b1c8a5fbf","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ZfcTopo8BaireCategorySpace}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[58-df-zfc-topo8-baire-category-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-baire-property","status":"resolved","id":"b5b9f71b20826f2d","anchor":"ref-6","targ